{"abstract":[{"text":"Kirnberger II (Johann Philipp Kirnberger, c. 1771).","type":"text"}],"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning","doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/TuningSystem"]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["macOS"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"static"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"kirnbergerII"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"WellTemperament","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/WellTemperament","preciseIdentifier":"s:10IvorTuning15WellTemperamentV"},{"kind":"text","text":" { "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"get"},{"text":" }","kind":"text"}],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"discussion","text":"Discussion","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Two fifths — D→A and A→E — are each narrowed by ½ of the syntonic comma, equal to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"√(20\/9) ≈ 691.202 cents. One fifth — F♯→C♯ — is narrowed by one schisma","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(32805:32768), equal to 16384:10935 ≈ 699.977 cents. The remaining nine fifths are","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"pure (3:2). The circle closes exactly because one syntonic comma times one schisma","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"equals one Pythagorean comma.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The two half-comma fifths are unusually flat, giving C-adjacent keys very pure"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"thirds while keys with many sharps or flats suffer greatly."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/ivortuning\/tuningsystem\/kirnbergerii"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/IvorTun